  "about": "THE LANE'S TWO ENGINES ARE ONE BEHAVIOUR (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-terminal-lane-design.md §5). Each scenario runs two engines over the test pipe — host/streaming-engine/PionBridge/rdev_lane_engine_test.go (TestTheEnginesAgreePacketForPacket) and web/test/lane.test.ts ('the engines agree packet for packet') — and hashes every packet each side emits, in order: SHA-256 over (at u32 · lost u8 · len u16 · bytes) per packet, big-endian, with the first 16 hex digits of the running hash after every checkpointEvery packets as checkpoints (the first that differs brackets the first diverging packet). The pipe draws from one generator (mulberry32) in one order in both languages, so a seed is one run. NOT GENERATED BY A THIRD IMPLEMENTATION: an engine change that moves a digest is pasted in from the failing suite's message, in the same commit, and the OTHER suite must then pass unchanged — a digest that moves must move in both languages together. Traffic: message i of an entry is the pipes' test message (stream, i, base + (i·mul) mod m bytes), sent once the clock reaches at + i·every; zeroRoom: a side's polls get no room in [from, to).",
